Commands used in GIT as of now

--> git add = To add the content of the file from working copy to to staging area (untracked)
--> git commit -m " message "  = To add the content of the file from staging area to local repo (new commit id will get created once we commited)


--> git remote add origin https://github.com/learningdevops77/shetty.git (your git hub link) = To add your local repo
to remote repository
--> git push origin master(branch name) = Which is used to push the branch from local to remote repository
(after entering the above command we need to give the user name and passcode (to get passcode we need to go to the 
top right corner icon and developer one and generate the classic passcode)

--> git branch = To see the branches 
git--> git checkout branch name = To change the branch

<This are the commands learned in git>
 
